(function(E){ const x = E["exam-08"] = E["exam-08"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x08-r1"] = {"id":"x08-r1","patterns":["RA-history","GT1-reviews","GT1-ads","PARA-cause","TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge","TR-paraphrase","TR-limit","TR-plural","TR-samewords","TR-detail"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes on a person’s life with words from the passage, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN by checking each statement against one place in the text.","tr":"Bu derste bir kişinin hayatıyla ilgili notları metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve her ifadeyi metindeki tek bir yerle karşılaştırarak TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌های مربوط به زندگی یک نفر را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی و با مقایسه‌ی هر جمله با یک جای مشخص در متن، بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match statements to short reviews quickly, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on an advert for an activity centre.","tr":"Bu derste ifadeleri kısa yorumlarla hızla eşleştirmeyi ve bir aktivite merkezi ilanında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را سریع با نظرهای کوتاه جور کنی و درباره‌ی آگهی یک مرکز تفریحی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: a biography","tr":"Reading Passage 1: bir biyografi","fa":"Reading Passage 1: یک زندگی‌نامه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes on a person’s life with words from the passage, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN by checking each statement against one place in the text.","tr":"Bu derste bir kişinin hayatıyla ilgili notları metindeki kelimelerle tamamlamayı ve her ifadeyi metindeki tek bir yerle karşılaştırarak TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌های مربوط به زندگی یک نفر را با کلمه‌های متن کامل کنی و با مقایسه‌ی هر جمله با یک جای مشخص در متن، بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~800"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a textile designer","tr":"Bu sınav: bir tekstil tasarımcısı","fa":"این آزمون: یک طراح پارچه"},"intro":{"en":"Academic Passage 1 is usually a clear factual account in time order. History and biography are among the most frequent topics. Learn the paraphrases on the card: the notes and statements rarely use the passage’s own words.","tr":"Academic Passage 1 genelde zaman sırasına göre açık ve bilgilendirici bir anlatımdır. Tarih ve biyografi en sık çıkan konulardandır. Karttaki eş anlamlıları öğren: notlar ve ifadeler metnin kendi kelimelerini nadiren kullanır.","fa":"Academic Passage 1 معمولاً روایتی روشن و واقعی به ترتیب زمان است. تاریخ و زندگی‌نامه از پرتکرارترین موضوع‌هایند. معادل‌های کارت را یاد بگیر: یادداشت‌ها و جمله‌ها به‌ندرت کلمه‌های خودِ متن را به کار می‌برند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x08-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-history","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"The life and work of a designer","tr":"Bir tasarımcının hayatı ve işleri","fa":"زندگی و کار یک طراح"},"asks":{"en":"A biography in time order: early life, training, a difficult start, the work that made the person famous, later work and how they are seen today. The notes follow the stages of the life; the statements test details such as who, when and whether something continued.","tr":"Zaman sırasına göre bir biyografi: çocukluk, eğitim, zor bir başlangıç, kişiyi ünlü yapan iş, sonraki işler ve bugün nasıl görüldüğü. Notlar hayatın aşamalarını izler; ifadeler kim, ne zaman, bir şeyin devam edip etmediği gibi ayrıntıları ölçer.","fa":"یک زندگی‌نامه به ترتیب زمان: کودکی، آموزش، شروعی سخت، کاری که آن آدم را مشهور کرد، کارهای بعدی و اینکه امروز چطور دیده می‌شود. یادداشت‌ها مرحله‌های زندگی را دنبال می‌کنند؛ جمله‌ها جزئیاتی مثل چه کسی، کی و اینکه چیزی ادامه پیدا کرد یا نه را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Family and early life","Training","Early career","The famous work","Later work","Reputation today"],"words":[{"a":"trained as","b":"studied / specialised in","tr":"... olarak eğitim aldı","fa":"آموزش ... دید"},{"a":"earned a living","b":"worked as / supported herself by","tr":"geçimini sağladı","fa":"خرجش را درآورد"},{"a":"designed to match","b":"to go with / to suit","tr":"uyumlu olsun diye tasarlandı","fa":"برای هماهنگی طراحی شد"},{"a":"based on","b":"inspired by / drawn from","tr":"... temel alınarak","fa":"بر پایه‌ی"},{"a":"doubted","b":"were unsure / feared that","tr":"şüphe ettiler","fa":"شک داشتند"},{"a":"proved wrong","b":"it turned out otherwise / they were mistaken","tr":"yanıldıkları ortaya çıktı","fa":"ثابت شد اشتباه می‌کردند"},{"a":"won a prize","b":"was given an award / a medal","tr":"ödül kazandı","fa":"جایزه برد"},{"a":"copied","b":"imitated / followed","tr":"taklit edildi","fa":"تقلید شد"},{"a":"at the same time","b":"continued to / alongside","tr":"aynı zamanda","fa":"هم‌زمان"},{"a":"one-off","b":"made only once / not mass-produced","tr":"tek örnek","fa":"تک‌نسخه‌ای"},{"a":"turned to","b":"moved into / began a new kind of work","tr":"... yöneldi","fa":"رو آورد به"},{"a":"better known to experts","b":"little known to the public","tr":"uzmanlarca daha çok bilinen","fa":"بیشتر در میان متخصص‌ها شناخته‌شده"}],"traps":[{"en":"A statement compares two things (\"more than any other\"), but the passage only describes one. That is NOT GIVEN, not TRUE.","tr":"Bir ifade iki şeyi karşılaştırır (\"diğerlerinden daha çok\") ama metin yalnızca birini anlatır. Bu TRUE değil, NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"جمله دو چیز را مقایسه می‌کند («بیشتر از هر چیز دیگر»)، اما متن فقط یکی را توصیف می‌کند. این NOT GIVEN است، نه TRUE."},{"en":"\"Stopped\" against \"continued\": if the passage says she did both at the same time, a statement saying she stopped is FALSE.","tr":"\"Bıraktı\" ile \"devam etti\": metin ikisini aynı anda yaptığını söylüyorsa \"bıraktı\" diyen ifade FALSE’tur.","fa":"«متوقف کرد» در برابر «ادامه داد»: اگر متن می‌گوید هر دو را هم‌زمان انجام داد، جمله‌ای که می‌گوید متوقف کرد FALSE است."},{"en":"Gap answers must be copied in the passage’s form: if it says \"textiles\", the plural is part of the answer.","tr":"Boşluk cevapları metindeki biçimiyle kopyalanmalı: metin \"textiles\" diyorsa çoğul cevabın parçasıdır.","fa":"جواب جای خالی باید به همان شکل متن کپی شود: اگر متن «textiles» می‌گوید، جمع بودن جزء جواب است."}],"example":{"text":"\"The architect worked for the city council for ten years, while also teaching evening classes.\"","item":"Statement: The architect gave up teaching when she joined the council.","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"While also teaching\" = she did both, so she did not give up teaching.","tr":"\"Bir yandan da ders verirken\" = ikisini birlikte yaptı; yani öğretmenliği bırakmadı.","fa":"«در حالی که درس هم می‌داد» یعنی هر دو را انجام می‌داد، پس تدریس را کنار نگذاشت."}}},{"id":"RA-history-p1","ctx":["RA-history"],"title":{"en":"The history of an object, a place or a trade","tr":"Bir nesnenin, yerin ya da ticaretin tarihi","fa":"تاریخچه‌ی یک شیء، یک مکان یا یک تجارت"},"asks":{"en":"The history of an everyday object, a trade, a building or a discovery: where it began, who developed it, how it spread and how it changed. Statements test dates, people and causes; the notes follow the order of events.","tr":"Gündelik bir nesnenin, bir ticaretin, bir binanın ya da bir keşfin tarihi: nerede başladığı, kimin geliştirdiği, nasıl yayıldığı ve nasıl değiştiği. İfadeler tarihleri, kişileri ve nedenleri sınar; notlar olayların sırasını izler.","fa":"تاریخچه‌ی یک شیء روزمره، یک تجارت، یک ساختمان یا یک کشف: از کجا شروع شد، چه کسی آن را توسعه داد، چطور گسترش یافت و چطور تغییر کرد. جمله‌ها تاریخ‌ها، آدم‌ها و علت‌ها را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب رویدادها را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The material was first used by local farmers.","The design changed in the 18th century.","The inventor made a lot of money from it.","Notes: Origins · Early uses · Spread · Later developments"],"words":[{"a":"invented","b":"developed / came up with","tr":"icat etti","fa":"اختراع کرد"},{"a":"popular","b":"in demand / widely used","tr":"rağbet gören","fa":"پرطرفدار"},{"a":"spread","b":"was taken to / reached","tr":"yayıldı","fa":"گسترش یافت"},{"a":"expensive","b":"costly / only the rich could afford it","tr":"pahalı","fa":"گران"},{"a":"replaced","b":"took the place of / gave way to","tr":"yerini aldı","fa":"جایش را گرفت"},{"a":"soon","b":"within a few years / shortly afterwards","tr":"kısa sürede","fa":"به‌زودی"},{"a":"earlier than","b":"predates / came before","tr":"... -den önce","fa":"زودتر از"},{"a":"made money","b":"profited from / earned","tr":"para kazandı","fa":"پول درآورد"},{"a":"the government","b":"the authorities / the state","tr":"hükümet","fa":"دولت"},{"a":"exported","b":"sold abroad","tr":"ihraç etti","fa":"صادر کرد"},{"a":"remained","b":"continued / was still","tr":"kaldı, sürdü","fa":"باقی ماند"},{"a":"by hand","b":"without machines / manually","tr":"elle","fa":"با دست"}],"traps":[{"en":"NOT GIVEN when the text names a person but says nothing about their money, motives or feelings.","tr":"Metin bir kişinin adını verip parası, amacı ya da duyguları hakkında hiçbir şey söylemiyorsa: NOT GIVEN.","fa":"وقتی متن اسم کسی را می‌آورد ولی درباره‌ی پول، انگیزه یا احساسش چیزی نمی‌گوید: NOT GIVEN."},{"en":"Dates close together: \"first described in 1565, made in factories from 1795\". Match the date to the event.","tr":"Yakın tarihler: \"ilk kez 1565’te tarif edildi, 1795’ten itibaren fabrikada üretildi\". Tarihi olayla eşleştir.","fa":"تاریخ‌های نزدیک هم: «اولین بار ۱۵۶۵ توصیف شد، از ۱۷۹۵ در کارخانه ساخته شد». تاریخ را با رویداد جور کن."}],"example":{"text":"Glass windows were known in Roman times, but for centuries only churches and the very rich could afford them. In 1696 England introduced a tax on windows, and many owners bricked theirs up. The tax was finally abolished in 1851.","item":"Notes: Window tax: introduced in ___   (ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER)","answer":"1696","why":{"en":"1696 is when it was introduced; 1851 is when it was abolished.","tr":"1696 getirildiği yıl; 1851 kaldırıldığı yıl.","fa":"۱۶۹۶ سال وضع مالیات است؛ ۱۸۵۱ سال لغو آن."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-history"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Seven notes, then six statements","tr":"Yedi not, sonra altı ifade","fa":"هفت یادداشت، بعد شش جمله"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: complete notes with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Questions 8-13: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Both sets follow the order of the passage. Spend about 20 minutes; there is no extra time to copy answers.","tr":"Soru 1-7: notları metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. Soru 8-13: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. İki grup da metnin sırasını izler. Yaklaşık 20 dakika ayır; cevapları aktarmak için ek süre yok.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: یادداشت‌ها را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۳: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN. هر دو گروه به ترتیب متن جلو می‌روند. حدود ۲۰ دقیقه وقت بگذار؛ زمان اضافه برای انتقال جواب‌ها نیست."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Use the note headings and any dates or names to find the right paragraph.","tr":"Doğru paragrafı bulmak için not başlıklarını, tarihleri ve isimleri kullan.","fa":"برای پیدا کردن پاراگراف درست از عنوان یادداشت‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و اسم‌ها کمک بگیر."},{"en":"Find the paraphrase of the words around the gap and copy one word in the passage’s form.","tr":"Boşluğun etrafındaki kelimelerin eş anlamlısını bul ve tek kelimeyi metindeki biçimiyle kopyala.","fa":"معادلِ کلمه‌های دور جای خالی را پیدا کن و یک کلمه را به همان شکلِ متن کپی کن."},{"en":"For each statement, find the one sentence it is about and compare every detail.","tr":"Her ifade için ilgili olduğu tek cümleyi bul ve her ayrıntıyı karşılaştır.","fa":"برای هر جمله، همان یک جمله‌ی مربوط در متن را پیدا کن و همه‌ی جزئیات را مقایسه کن."},{"en":"Watch words that change the meaning: both, only, stopped, continued, more than.","tr":"Anlamı değiştiren kelimelere dikkat et: both, only, stopped, continued, more than.","fa":"حواست به کلمه‌هایی باشد که معنی را عوض می‌کنند: both، only، stopped، continued، more than."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?","text":"\"The composer wrote eleven operas. The first was performed in Vienna in 1781 and was well received by the critics.\"","item":"Statement: The composer’s first opera was his most popular.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: \"The first was performed...\"","tr":"Yeri bul: \"The first was performed...\"","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: «The first was performed...»"},{"en":"Compare: \"well received by the critics\" tells us it was liked, not that it was the most popular of the eleven.","tr":"Karşılaştır: \"eleştirmenlerce iyi karşılandı\" sevildiğini söylüyor, on bir opera arasında en popüler olduğunu değil.","fa":"مقایسه کن: «منتقدها از آن استقبال کردند» می‌گوید پسندیده شد، نه اینکه محبوب‌ترینِ آن یازده اپرا بود."},{"en":"There is no comparison in the text: NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Metinde karşılaştırma yok: NOT GIVEN.","fa":"در متن مقایسه‌ای نیست: NOT GIVEN."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"After the war she returned to painting, although she never gave up her work as a translator.\" Statement: \"She stopped translating when she went back to painting.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Never gave up\" contradicts \"stopped\": FALSE.","tr":"\"Asla bırakmadı\", \"bıraktı\" ile çelişiyor: FALSE.","fa":"«هرگز کنار نگذاشت» با «متوقف کرد» تناقض دارد: FALSE."}},"remember":{"en":"One statement, one sentence in the text. Opposite = FALSE; a point the text never makes = NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Bir ifade, metinde bir cümle. Tersi = FALSE; metnin hiç söylemediği bir nokta = NOT GIVEN.","fa":"یک جمله، یک جای متن. برعکس = FALSE؛ نکته‌ای که متن هیچ‌وقت نمی‌گوید = NOT GIVEN."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x08-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"Lucienne Day: patterns for everyday life","tr":"Lucienne Day: gündelik hayat için desenler","fa":"لوسیِن دی: طرح‌هایی برای زندگی روزمره"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-history"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"Lucienne Day: patterns for everyday life\n\nIn the years after the Second World War, many British homes were dark, crowded and badly in need of repair. Within a decade, however, a new style of interior had appeared in shops and magazines: light, cheerful and modern. Few people did more to create it than Lucienne Day, a designer whose printed fabrics turned abstract art into something ordinary families could hang at their windows.\n\nShe was born Désirée Lucienne Conradi in 1917, in a suburb south of London. Her father, a Belgian, worked in insurance, and her mother was English. As a girl she was more interested in drawing and colour than in schoolwork, and at seventeen she enrolled at Croydon School of Art. It was there, while experimenting with printing on cloth, that she realised she wanted to design for a living rather than to paint.\n\nIn 1937 she won a place at the Royal College of Art in London, where she specialised in printed textiles. The college was then dominated by traditional ideas about pattern, and students were expected to copy historical designs. Day found this frustrating. She was far more excited by modern painting, and she spent much of her free time looking at exhibitions. In her final year she met Robin Day, another student at the college, who was training to design furniture. They married in 1942.\n\nThe war made it almost impossible to start a career in design. Factories were producing goods for the armed forces, and decorative fabrics were barely made at all. For several years Lucienne Day worked as a teacher at a small art school, while she and her husband shared a flat that doubled as a studio. Even so, she continued to draw constantly, filling notebooks with ideas for patterns that no one could yet afford to print. When she could find a buyer, she also sold small designs for dress fabrics, which taught her how quickly a pattern has to catch the eye in a shop.\n\nHer opportunity came in 1951 with the Festival of Britain, a national exhibition intended to show a country recovering from war. Robin Day had been asked to design rooms for one of the pavilions, and Lucienne produced a fabric to go with his furniture. She called it Calyx, after the green cup that holds the petals of a flower. The design was made up of spindly lines and cup-like shapes in mustard, orange and black on an earthy background. Its forms were inspired by the stems and cups of flowers, but they were drawn so freely that many people saw them simply as abstract shapes.\n\nThe design was printed by Heal's, a London furniture shop with its own fabric business. The firm's directors were unsure about it at first; they doubted that customers would buy anything so unusual, and they paid her only a modest fee. They were proved wrong. Calyx won a gold medal at an international design exhibition in Milan in 1951, and an American award the following year. More importantly, it sold steadily for years and was widely imitated. Before long, department stores were full of fabrics with similar thin lines and plant-like forms.\n\nOver the next two decades Day designed dozens of fabrics for Heal's, together with wallpapers, carpets and table linen for other manufacturers. From the late 1950s she also worked for a German company, decorating porcelain, and she continued to produce textiles for Heal's at the same time. Her patterns changed with the period, becoming bolder and more geometric in the 1960s, but they always had the same lively, carefully balanced quality. She believed strongly that good design should not be a luxury, and she was pleased that people with modest incomes could own her work.\n\nBy the 1970s, however, the market for printed furnishing fabrics had changed. Manufacturers were cutting costs, and Day felt that the industry no longer valued original design. She turned instead to a new form that she called silk mosaics: large wall hangings assembled from hundreds of small pieces of silk, carefully cut and sewn together. These were one-off works rather than products for mass production, and some were made for public buildings, including offices and churches. She later said that this period gave her a freedom she had never had while designing for factories.\n\nLucienne Day died in 2010, at the age of ninety-three. For many years her name had been better known to specialists than to the general public, perhaps because she always worked in the shadow of commercial firms. Recent exhibitions have changed this, and her early designs are now reprinted and sold again. Seen today, Calyx may look like a period piece, but in 1951 it was a clear sign that ordinary homes were ready for something new.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Lucienne Day","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Training · at the Royal College of Art her main subject was printed ___","accept":["textiles"],"limit":1,"evidence":"where she specialised in printed textiles","why":{"en":"\"Specialised in\" = her main subject. Copy the plural: textiles.","tr":"\"Specialised in\" = ana dalı. Çoğulu aynen yaz: textiles.","fa":"«specialised in» یعنی رشته‌ی اصلی‌اش. جمع را کپی کن: textiles."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-plural"]},{"n":2,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The war years · earned a living as a ___ at a small art school","accept":["teacher"],"limit":1,"evidence":"worked as a teacher at a small art school","why":{"en":"\"Worked as a teacher\" = earned a living as a teacher.","tr":"\"Öğretmen olarak çalıştı\" = geçimini öğretmenlikle sağladı.","fa":"«به‌عنوان معلم کار کرد» یعنی از راه معلمی خرج زندگی‌اش را درمی‌آورد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Calyx · designed to match her husband’s ___","accept":["furniture"],"limit":1,"evidence":"to go with his furniture","why":{"en":"\"To go with his furniture\" = to match it.","tr":"\"Onun mobilyalarıyla uyumlu olsun diye\" = onlara uyacak şekilde.","fa":"«تا با مبلمان او جور باشد» یعنی هماهنگ با آن."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Calyx · its shapes were based on parts of ___","accept":["flowers"],"limit":1,"evidence":"inspired by the stems and cups of flowers","why":{"en":"\"Inspired by the stems and cups of flowers\". Keep the plural.","tr":"\"Çiçeklerin saplarından ve çanaklarından esinlenmiş\". Çoğulu koru.","fa":"«الهام‌گرفته از ساقه‌ها و کاسه‌ی گل‌ها». جمع را نگه دار."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":5,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Calyx · Heal’s directors thought it was too ___ to sell","accept":["unusual"],"limit":1,"evidence":"they doubted that customers would buy anything so unusual","why":{"en":"They doubted customers \"would buy anything so unusual\".","tr":"Müşterilerin \"bu kadar alışılmadık bir şeyi\" alacağından şüphe ettiler.","fa":"شک داشتند مشتری‌ها «چیزی به این عجیبی» را بخرند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Later work · decorated ___ for a company in Germany","accept":["porcelain"],"limit":1,"evidence":"decorating porcelain","why":{"en":"\"She also worked for a German company, decorating porcelain.\"","tr":"\"Bir Alman şirketi için porselen süsledi.\"","fa":"«برای یک شرکت آلمانی ظروف چینی را تزئین می‌کرد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Later work · wall hangings sewn together from small pieces of ___","accept":["silk"],"limit":1,"evidence":"hundreds of small pieces of silk","why":{"en":"\"Assembled from hundreds of small pieces of silk\": one word.","tr":"\"Yüzlerce küçük ipek parçasından yapılmış\": tek kelime.","fa":"«از صدها تکه‌ی کوچک ابریشم سرهم شده»: یک کلمه."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 8-13. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Both of Lucienne Day’s parents were English.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Her father, a Belgian, worked in insurance","why":{"en":"Her father was Belgian, so not both parents were English.","tr":"Babası Belçikalıydı; yani ikisi de İngiliz değildi.","fa":"پدرش بلژیکی بود، پس هر دو انگلیسی نبودند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Day met her future husband while they were studying at the same college.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"she met Robin Day, another student at the college","why":{"en":"\"Another student at the college\" = they were both studying there.","tr":"\"Kolejde başka bir öğrenci\" = ikisi de orada okuyordu.","fa":"«دانشجوی دیگری در همان کالج» یعنی هر دو آن‌جا درس می‌خواندند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Calyx sold more copies than any other fabric produced by Heal’s.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"it sold steadily for years and was widely imitated","why":{"en":"It \"sold steadily\", but there is no comparison with Heal’s other fabrics.","tr":"\"İstikrarlı biçimde satıldı\" ama Heal’s’in diğer kumaşlarıyla bir karşılaştırma yok.","fa":"«به‌طور پیوسته فروش رفت»، اما مقایسه‌ای با پارچه‌های دیگر هیلز نشده."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Calyx won a prize in a country other than Britain.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"won a gold medal at an international design exhibition in Milan","why":{"en":"A gold medal in Milan, and an American award: prizes outside Britain.","tr":"Milano’da altın madalya ve bir Amerikan ödülü: Britanya dışında ödüller.","fa":"مدال طلا در میلان و یک جایزه‌ی آمریکایی: جایزه‌هایی بیرون از بریتانیا."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Day stopped designing fabrics for Heal’s when she started working on porcelain.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"she continued to produce textiles for Heal's at the same time","why":{"en":"\"At the same time\": she did both.","tr":"\"Aynı zamanda\": ikisini birlikte yaptı.","fa":"«هم‌زمان»: هر دو کار را انجام می‌داد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Day earned more from her silk mosaics than from her printed fabrics.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"These were one-off works rather than products for mass production","why":{"en":"The passage says the mosaics were one-off works that gave her freedom; it says nothing about how much she earned.","tr":"Metin mozaiklerin ona özgürlük veren tek örnek işler olduğunu söylüyor; ne kadar kazandığından söz etmiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید موزاییک‌ها کارهای تک‌نسخه‌ای بودند که به او آزادی دادند؛ درباره‌ی درآمدش چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]}]}],"id":"c-x08-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The design was widely imitated.\" This means other designers...","options":["criticised it","copied it","bought it"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"To imitate = to copy.","tr":"Imitate = taklit etmek, kopyalamak.","fa":"imitate یعنی تقلید کردن، کپی کردن."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A note says \"her main subject was ___\". Which phrase in a passage would you look for?","options":["she specialised in","she was interested in","she later taught"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Specialised in\" = the main subject of her studies.","tr":"\"Specialised in\" = eğitiminin ana konusu.","fa":"«specialised in» یعنی موضوع اصلی درسش."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Notes: \"ONE WORD ONLY from the passage\". The passage says \"the walls were decorated with images of birds\". Gap: \"decorations showing ___\". You write...","options":["bird","the birds","birds"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Copy the word in the passage’s form, with its plural.","tr":"Kelimeyi metindeki biçimiyle, çoğul ekiyle kopyala.","fa":"کلمه را به همان شکلِ متن، با جمعش، کپی کن."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"The novel was translated into several languages.\" Statement: \"The novel was more successful abroad than at home.\"","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Translation is mentioned, but no comparison of success.","tr":"Çeviriden söz ediliyor ama başarı karşılaştırması yok.","fa":"از ترجمه حرف زده شده، اما مقایسه‌ای درباره‌ی موفقیت نیست."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"He kept his job at the bank throughout his career as a poet.\" Statement: \"He left the bank to write poetry.\"","options":["FALSE","TRUE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Kept his job throughout\" contradicts \"left\".","tr":"\"Kariyeri boyunca işini sürdürdü\", \"ayrıldı\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«در تمام دوران شاعری‌اش کارش را نگه داشت» با «ترک کرد» تناقض دارد."}}],"id":"c-x08-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: reviews and an advert","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: yorumlar ve bir ilan","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: نظرها و یک آگهی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match statements to short reviews quickly, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on an advert for an activity centre.","tr":"Bu derste ifadeleri kısa yorumlarla hızla eşleştirmeyi ve bir aktivite merkezi ilanında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را سریع با نظرهای کوتاه جور کنی و درباره‌ی آگهی یک مرکز تفریحی بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"about 20 min","tr":"yaklaşık 20 dk","fa":"حدود ۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: walking boots and a kayak centre","tr":"Bu sınav: yürüyüş botları ve bir kano merkezi","fa":"این آزمون: پوتین کوهپیمایی و یک مرکز کایاک"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 1 uses short everyday texts. Reviews and adverts are two of the most frequent kinds. The language is simple, but the questions paraphrase every detail.","tr":"GT Section 1 kısa günlük metinler kullanır. Yorumlar ve ilanlar en sık çıkan iki türdür. Dil basittir ama sorular her ayrıntıyı başka kelimelerle söyler.","fa":"GT Section 1 از متن‌های کوتاه روزمره استفاده می‌کند. نظرها و آگهی‌ها دو نوعِ پرتکرارند. زبان ساده است، اما سؤال‌ها همه‌ی جزئیات را با کلمه‌های دیگر می‌گویند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x08-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews","GT1-ads"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Product reviews and a leisure advert","tr":"Ürün yorumları ve bir eğlence ilanı","fa":"نظرهای مشتری‌ها و یک آگهی تفریحی"},"asks":{"en":"First, six short reviews of the same kind of product, lettered A-F: you decide which review each statement is about. Then an advert for an activity centre: you decide whether each statement is TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Önce aynı türden bir ürünün A-F harfli altı kısa yorumu: her ifadenin hangi yorumla ilgili olduğuna karar veriyorsun. Sonra bir aktivite merkezinin ilanı: her ifadenin TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olduğuna karar veriyorsun.","fa":"اول شش نظر کوتاه درباره‌ی یک نوع کالا با حرف‌های A تا F: تصمیم می‌گیری هر جمله درباره‌ی کدام نظر است. بعد آگهی یک مرکز تفریحی: تصمیم می‌گیری هر جمله TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است."},"fields":["Comfort","Weight","Fit and size","Price","Guarantee","Age limits","Booking and deposits","Cancellations"],"words":[{"a":"comfortable at once","b":"no breaking in / felt fine from day one","tr":"hemen rahat","fa":"از همان اول راحت"},{"a":"light","b":"weigh very little / you hardly notice them","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"},{"a":"narrow","b":"cut slim / tight across the foot","tr":"dar","fa":"باریک، تنگ"},{"a":"cheap","b":"half price / in the sale / good value","tr":"ucuz","fa":"ارزان"},{"a":"will last","b":"a long guarantee / built to last","tr":"dayanıklı","fa":"دوام می‌آورد"},{"a":"waterproof","b":"keeps water out / dry feet","tr":"su geçirmez","fa":"ضدآب"},{"a":"accompanied by","b":"must come with / with a paying adult","tr":"... eşliğinde","fa":"همراهِ"},{"a":"at short notice","b":"with little warning","tr":"kısa süre önce haber vererek","fa":"با اطلاع کوتاه"},{"a":"refund","b":"your money back","tr":"para iadesi","fa":"پس گرفتن پول"},{"a":"free of charge","b":"provided at no cost / included","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"in advance","b":"beforehand / at least a week before","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"a discount","b":"money off / pay less","tr":"indirim","fa":"تخفیف"}],"traps":[{"en":"The same word in two reviews: two reviews may say \"light\" or \"wet\", but only one matches the whole statement.","tr":"İki yorumda aynı kelime: iki yorum \"light\" ya da \"wet\" diyebilir ama ifadenin tamamına yalnızca biri uyar.","fa":"یک کلمه در دو نظر: ممکن است دو نظر «light» یا «wet» بگویند، اما فقط یکی با کل جمله جور است."},{"en":"An advert mentions a meal stop, a car park or equipment without saying who pays or how often. A statement that adds that detail is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Bir ilan bir yemek molasından, otoparktan ya da ekipmandan söz eder ama kimin ödediğini ya da ne sıklıkla olduğunu söylemez. Bu ayrıntıyı ekleyen ifade NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"آگهی از توقف برای غذا، پارکینگ یا وسایل حرف می‌زند، بی‌آنکه بگوید چه کسی پولش را می‌دهد یا هر چند وقت. جمله‌ای که این جزئیات را اضافه می‌کند NOT GIVEN است."}],"example":{"text":"A  \"Warm and dry all day, though they cost a fortune.\"  B  \"Bought these cheaply online; my socks were wet by lunchtime.\"","item":"Which boots let water in?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"B: wet socks by lunchtime. A mentions \"dry\", which is the opposite.","tr":"B: öğlene kadar çoraplar ıslak. A \"dry\" diyor, bu tam tersi.","fa":"B: تا ظهر جوراب‌ها خیس بود. A می‌گوید «dry» که برعکس است."}}},{"id":"GT1-reviews","ctx":["GT1-reviews"],"title":{"en":"Product and service reviews","tr":"Ürün ve hizmet değerlendirmeleri","fa":"نقد و معرفی کالا و خدمات"},"asks":{"en":"Short reviews or descriptions A-F of products or places: sleeping bags, kitchen machines, cafes, hotels, phone apps. Questions ask which one has a feature, or which review says something.","tr":"Ürünler ya da yerler hakkında A-F harfli kısa değerlendirmeler veya tanıtımlar: uyku tulumları, mutfak aletleri, kafeler, oteller, telefon uygulamaları. Sorular hangisinin bir özelliği olduğunu ya da hangi yorumun bir şey söylediğini sorar.","fa":"نقدها یا معرفی‌های کوتاه A تا F درباره‌ی کالاها یا مکان‌ها: کیسه‌خواب، وسایل آشپزخانه، کافه، هتل، اپلیکیشن. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام یک ویژگی را دارد، یا کدام نقد چیزی را می‌گوید."},"fields":["Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","Which cafe has outdoor seating?","Which app works without the internet?","Which hotel is suitable for families?"],"words":[{"a":"lightweight","b":"weighs very little / easy to carry","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"},{"a":"durable","b":"lasts for years / hard-wearing","tr":"dayanıklı","fa":"بادوام"},{"a":"value for money","b":"a good price for what you get","tr":"fiyatına değer","fa":"به‌صرفه"},{"a":"noisy","b":"loud","tr":"gürültülü","fa":"پرسروصدا"},{"a":"spacious","b":"lots of room","tr":"ferah","fa":"جادار"},{"a":"easy to clean","b":"wipes clean","tr":"kolay temizlenir","fa":"راحت تمیز می‌شود"},{"a":"offline","b":"without an internet connection","tr":"çevrimdışı","fa":"آفلاین"},{"a":"outdoor seating","b":"tables outside","tr":"dışarıda oturma yeri","fa":"میز در فضای باز"},{"a":"guarantee","b":"free repairs for two years","tr":"garanti","fa":"گارانتی"},{"a":"compact","b":"small / takes up little space","tr":"küçük, kompakt","fa":"جمع‌وجور"},{"a":"fully booked","b":"no rooms left","tr":"tamamen dolu","fa":"کاملاً پر"},{"a":"suitable for families","b":"children welcome / cots available","tr":"ailelere uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Superlatives: \"the lightest\" needs a comparison with all the others, not just the word \"light\".","tr":"Üstünlük sıfatları: \"en hafif\" diğerlerinin hepsiyle karşılaştırma ister, yalnızca \"hafif\" kelimesi yetmez.","fa":"صفت عالی: «سبک‌ترین» یعنی مقایسه با همه‌ی بقیه، نه فقط کلمه‌ی «سبک»."},{"en":"A review may mention a feature only to say that it is missing.","tr":"Bir yorum bir özellikten yalnızca eksik olduğunu söylemek için bahsedebilir.","fa":"یک نقد ممکن است به ویژگی‌ای فقط اشاره کند تا بگوید ندارد."}],"example":{"text":"A  The Trekker 200 weighs 900 g and packs down small.\nB  The Summit weighs just 650 g, though it is not quite as warm.\nC  The Polar Pro is the warmest of the three, at 1.4 kg.","item":"Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Compare all three: 650 g is less than 900 g and 1.4 kg.","tr":"Üçünü de karşılaştır: 650 g, 900 g ve 1,4 kg’dan az.","fa":"هر سه را مقایسه کن: ۶۵۰ گرم از ۹۰۰ گرم و ۱٫۴ کیلو کمتر است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT1-ads","ctx":["GT1-ads"],"title":{"en":"Adverts and listings","tr":"İlanlar ve listeler","fa":"آگهی‌ها و فهرست‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"Short adverts or listings A-F for courses, events, campsites, tours or clubs. Questions ask which advert mentions a fact, or whether a statement is TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Kurslar, etkinlikler, kamp alanları, turlar ya da kulüpler için A-F harfli kısa ilanlar veya listeler. Sorular hangi ilanın bir bilgiden söz ettiğini ya da bir ifadenin TRUE, FALSE veya NOT GIVEN olduğunu sorar.","fa":"آگهی‌ها یا فهرست‌های کوتاه A تا F برای کلاس‌ها، رویدادها، کمپ‌ها، تورها یا باشگاه‌ها. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام آگهی به یک نکته اشاره می‌کند، یا یک جمله TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است."},"fields":["Which course is suitable for complete beginners?","Which event takes place outdoors?","Which campsite allows dogs?","Booking is required for all tours."],"words":[{"a":"suitable for beginners","b":"no experience needed","tr":"yeni başlayanlara uygun","fa":"مناسب مبتدی‌ها"},{"a":"free of charge","b":"at no cost / complimentary","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"booking essential","b":"places must be reserved","tr":"rezervasyon şart","fa":"رزرو الزامی"},{"a":"reduced price","b":"discount / 20% off","tr":"indirimli fiyat","fa":"قیمت با تخفیف"},{"a":"family-friendly","b":"children welcome","tr":"aileye uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"},{"a":"outdoors","b":"in the open air","tr":"açık havada","fa":"در فضای باز"},{"a":"pets allowed","b":"dogs welcome","tr":"evcil hayvan kabul edilir","fa":"ورود حیوان خانگی آزاد"},{"a":"on site","b":"at the campsite itself","tr":"tesis içinde","fa":"در خود محل"},{"a":"equipment provided","b":"everything supplied","tr":"ekipman sağlanır","fa":"تجهیزات داده می‌شود"},{"a":"refundable","b":"money back if you cancel","tr":"iade edilebilir","fa":"قابل استرداد"},{"a":"weekly","b":"once a week","tr":"haftalık","fa":"هفتگی"},{"a":"within walking distance","b":"nearby / a short walk away","tr":"yürüme mesafesinde","fa":"با پای پیاده نزدیک"}],"traps":[{"en":"Matching: two adverts mention dogs, but only one allows them. Read the whole line.","tr":"Eşleştirme: iki ilan köpeklerden söz eder ama yalnızca biri izin verir. Satırın tamamını oku.","fa":"جورکردن: دو آگهی از سگ حرف می‌زنند، ولی فقط یکی اجازه می‌دهد. کل خط را بخوان."},{"en":"\"Free\" in one advert may mean free parking, not free entry.","tr":"Bir ilandaki \"free\" giriş değil, ücretsiz otopark anlamına gelebilir.","fa":"«free» در یک آگهی شاید یعنی پارکینگ رایگان، نه ورود رایگان."}],"example":{"text":"C  Lakeside Campsite. Quiet site by the water. Sorry, no dogs. Shop on site.\nD  Hilltop Farm Camping. Families and well-behaved pets welcome. Nearest shop 2 km.","item":"Which campsite allows dogs?","answer":"D","why":{"en":"Both mention dogs or pets. C says \"no dogs\"; D says \"pets welcome\".","tr":"İkisi de köpek ya da evcil hayvandan söz ediyor. C \"köpek yok\", D \"evcil hayvanlar kabul\" diyor.","fa":"هر دو از سگ یا حیوان خانگی حرف می‌زنند. C می‌گوید «سگ ممنوع»؛ D می‌گوید «حیوان خانگی پذیرفته می‌شود»."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-ads"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-ads","n":24,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 24 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 24’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۴ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"A box of reviews, then an advert","tr":"Bir yorum kutusu, sonra bir ilan","fa":"یک دسته نظر، بعد یک آگهی"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: write the letter of the review, A-F; a letter can be used more than once. Questions 8-14: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on the advert. Aim for about 20 minutes on this section.","tr":"Soru 1-7: yorumun harfini (A-F) yaz; bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 8-14: ilan hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Bu bölüme yaklaşık 20 dakika ayır.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: حرف نظر (A تا F) را بنویس؛ یک حرف را می‌شود بیش از یک بار به کار برد. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۴: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی آگهی. حدود ۲۰ دقیقه برای این بخش بگذار."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Skim the six reviews and give each a one-word label: light, cheap, leaks...","tr":"Altı yorumu göz gezdir ve her birine tek kelimelik bir etiket ver: hafif, ucuz, su alıyor...","fa":"شش نظر را سریع ببین و به هرکدام یک برچسب یک‌کلمه‌ای بده: سبک، ارزان، آب پس می‌دهد..."},{"en":"Read each statement, find the review with the same idea, and check the whole statement fits.","tr":"Her ifadeyi oku, aynı fikri taşıyan yorumu bul ve ifadenin tamamının uyduğunu kontrol et.","fa":"هر جمله را بخوان، نظری را که همان ایده را دارد پیدا کن و مطمئن شو کل جمله با آن جور است."},{"en":"For the advert, use headings to find the section, then compare the statement with one sentence.","tr":"İlan için başlıklarla bölümü bul, sonra ifadeyi tek bir cümleyle karşılaştır.","fa":"برای آگهی، با کمک عنوان‌ها بخش را پیدا کن و بعد جمله را با یک جمله‌ی متن مقایسه کن."},{"en":"Check numbers and limits: ages, days, prices and \"only\".","tr":"Sayıları ve sınırları kontrol et: yaşlar, günler, fiyatlar ve \"only\".","fa":"عددها و محدودیت‌ها را چک کن: سن، روز، قیمت و «only»."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"A matching word is not a match","tr":"Aynı kelime eşleşme demek değil","fa":"کلمه‌ی مشترک یعنی جور بودن نیست"},"body":{"en":"A statement like \"the reviewer was surprised by the weight\" needs both ideas: light AND surprised. A review that only says \"light\" is not enough.","tr":"\"Yorumcu ağırlığa şaşırdı\" gibi bir ifade iki fikri birden ister: hafif VE şaşırmış. Yalnızca \"light\" diyen bir yorum yetmez.","fa":"جمله‌ای مثل «نویسنده از وزنش تعجب کرد» هر دو ایده را می‌خواهد: سبک و تعجب. نظری که فقط می‌گوید «light» کافی نیست."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One advert statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ilan ifadesi, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله‌ی آگهی، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text?","text":"\"Helmets are provided. Riders under fourteen must be with a parent at all times.\"","item":"Statement: Thirteen-year-olds can ride on their own.","answer":"FALSE","walk":[{"en":"Find the rule about age: \"under fourteen\".","tr":"Yaşla ilgili kuralı bul: \"under fourteen\".","fa":"قانون مربوط به سن را پیدا کن: «under fourteen»."},{"en":"Thirteen is under fourteen, so they must be with a parent.","tr":"On üç, on dörtten küçük; yani bir ebeveynle olmalılar.","fa":"سیزده کمتر از چهارده است، پس باید با پدر یا مادر باشند."},{"en":"\"On their own\" is the opposite: FALSE.","tr":"\"Kendi başlarına\" tam tersi: FALSE.","fa":"«تنهایی» برعکس است: FALSE."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Lockers are available at reception.\" Statement: \"Lockers cost £1 a day.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The text says lockers exist, but nothing about the price.","tr":"Metin dolapların olduğunu söylüyor ama fiyattan söz etmiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید کمد هست، اما درباره‌ی قیمت چیزی نمی‌گوید."}},"remember":{"en":"Match the whole idea, not one word; in the advert, a detail the text never gives is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Tek bir kelimeyi değil, fikrin tamamını eşleştir; ilanda metnin hiç vermediği bir ayrıntı NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"کل ایده را جور کن، نه یک کلمه را؛ در آگهی، جزئیاتی که متن هرگز نمی‌دهد NOT GIVEN است."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x08-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"Walking boots and a kayak centre","tr":"Yürüyüş botları ve bir kano merkezi","fa":"پوتین کوهپیمایی و یک مرکز کایاک"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-reviews","GT1-ads"],"texts":[{"title":"Walking boots: what our readers say","kind":"reviews","body":"A  Ridgeline Trek\nI bought these for a week in the mountains and was ready for blisters, but they felt like slippers from the very first morning. No breaking in at all. The grip on wet rock is excellent. My only complaint is the colour: the bright orange shows every speck of mud.\n\nB  Kestrel Lite\nIdeal for long days on easy paths. When the parcel arrived I thought it must be empty, because the boots weigh so little. They are not the warmest, so I wear thick socks in winter. The laces are a little short, but that is easy to fix.\n\nC  Highmoor Classic\nA traditional leather boot that will last for years. The maker offers a five-year guarantee, which says a lot about its confidence. They took about three weeks of short walks before they stopped rubbing my heels, so do not take them on a long trip straight out of the box.\n\nD  Torrent GTX\nThe waterproof lining is the selling point, and for the first month it worked well. After that, my left foot was wet every time I crossed a stream. The shop agreed to replace them, but I have lost faith in the model. Comfortable, though, and good value.\n\nE  Summit Pro\nThese were half price in a January sale, otherwise I could never have afforded them. They are stiff and heavy, but on rough ground I have never felt so safe. Not a boot for a gentle stroll by the river.\n\nF  Meadow Walker\nA nice light boot for summer, and the soft soles are kind to your knees on hard tracks. However, they are cut very slim, so anyone who usually needs a wide fitting should look elsewhere. The laces wore through within a few weeks, but replacements are cheap."},{"title":"Saltmarsh Bay Kayak Centre: paddle with us this summer","kind":"promotion","body":"Whether you have never sat in a kayak or you are an experienced paddler, Saltmarsh Bay Kayak Centre has something for you this season.\n\nTaster sessions\nOur two-hour taster sessions run every Saturday and Sunday from May to September. They take place in the sheltered lagoon behind the beach, so the water is calm even on windy days. All equipment is included, and you only need to bring clothes that you do not mind getting wet. Participants must be at least eight years old, and children under sixteen must be accompanied by a paying adult.\n\nCoastal tours\nFor those with some experience, our guided coastal tours follow the cliffs to the sea caves at Gull Point. Tours last about four hours, including a stop for lunch on a small beach that can only be reached from the water. Please note that tours depend on the tides and the weather, and they may be cancelled at short notice. If this happens, you can choose a full refund or move to another date.\n\nHiring a kayak\nKayaks can be hired by the hour or by the day, but only by people who hold a recognised paddling certificate or who have completed one of our courses. Buoyancy aids must be worn at all times on the water, and the centre provides these free of charge.\n\nSafety\nAll our instructors hold national coaching qualifications and first-aid certificates. Before any session, you will be asked to complete a short health form. You do not need to be a strong swimmer, but you must be able to swim at least 50 metres.\n\nBooking\nPlaces on taster sessions can be booked online up to the day before. Tours must be booked at least a week in advance, and a deposit of £20 per person is required. Groups of eight or more receive a discount of ten per cent.\n\nGetting here\nThe centre is a five-minute walk from Saltmarsh Bay bus stop. Free parking is available for customers, but the car park is small, so please share cars where possible."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Look at the six reviews of walking boots, A-F. For which boots are the following statements true? Write the correct letter, A-F, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F"],"questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"match","prompt":"The reviewer was surprised at how light they are.","correct":1,"evidence":"I thought it must be empty","why":{"en":"B: the reviewer thought the parcel \"must be empty\". F is light too, but nobody is surprised.","tr":"B: yorumcu paketin \"boş olduğunu\" sandı. F de hafif ama kimse şaşırmıyor.","fa":"B: نویسنده خیال کرد بسته «حتماً خالی است». F هم سبک است، اما کسی تعجب نمی‌کند."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":2,"kind":"match","prompt":"They are not a good choice for people with wide feet.","correct":5,"evidence":"anyone who usually needs a wide fitting should look elsewhere","why":{"en":"F: \"cut very slim... should look elsewhere\".","tr":"F: \"çok dar kesim... başka yere bakmalı\".","fa":"F: «خیلی باریک دوخته شده... باید سراغ مدل دیگری برود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"match","prompt":"They need to be worn for some time before a long walk.","correct":2,"evidence":"They took about three weeks of short walks before they stopped rubbing my heels","why":{"en":"C: three weeks before they stopped rubbing; \"do not take them on a long trip straight out of the box\".","tr":"C: sürtmeyi bırakması üç hafta sürdü; \"kutudan çıkar çıkmaz uzun bir geziye götürmeyin\".","fa":"C: سه هفته طول کشید تا دیگر پاشنه را نساید؛ «همین که از جعبه درآوردی به سفر طولانی نبر»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"match","prompt":"The manufacturer promises they will last.","correct":2,"evidence":"The maker offers a five-year guarantee","why":{"en":"C again: \"a five-year guarantee\". A letter can be used twice.","tr":"Yine C: \"beş yıllık garanti\". Bir harf iki kez kullanılabilir.","fa":"باز هم C: «ضمانت پنج‌ساله». یک حرف را می‌شود دو بار به کار برد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"match","prompt":"They were bought at a reduced price.","correct":4,"evidence":"These were half price in a January sale","why":{"en":"E: \"half price in a January sale\". D is \"good value\", which is not the same.","tr":"E: \"ocak indiriminde yarı fiyatına\". D \"fiyatına göre iyi\", bu aynı şey değil.","fa":"E: «نصف قیمت در حراج ژانویه». D «ارزش قیمتش را دارد» که همان نیست."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":6,"kind":"match","prompt":"They stopped keeping water out.","correct":3,"evidence":"my left foot was wet every time I crossed a stream","why":{"en":"D: after a month the lining failed. A mentions wet rock, but only for grip.","tr":"D: bir ay sonra astar işe yaramaz oldu. A ıslak kayadan söz ediyor ama yalnızca tutuş için.","fa":"D: بعد از یک ماه آستر دیگر کار نکرد. A از سنگ خیس حرف می‌زند، اما فقط درباره‌ی چسبندگی."},"trap":["TR-samewords","TR-detail"]},{"n":7,"kind":"match","prompt":"They felt comfortable from the first day.","correct":0,"evidence":"they felt like slippers from the very first morning","why":{"en":"A: \"like slippers from the very first morning. No breaking in at all.\"","tr":"A: \"ilk sabahtan terlik gibi. Hiç alıştırma gerekmedi.\"","fa":"A: «از همان صبح اول مثل دمپایی بود. اصلاً نیازی به جاافتادن نداشت»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 8-14. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Taster sessions take place on the open sea.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"They take place in the sheltered lagoon behind the beach","why":{"en":"They are in a sheltered lagoon, not on the open sea.","tr":"Açık denizde değil, korunaklı bir lagünde yapılıyor.","fa":"در یک مرداب آرام و محافظت‌شده برگزار می‌شوند، نه در دریای باز."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"A twelve-year-old can do a taster session without an adult.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"children under sixteen must be accompanied by a paying adult","why":{"en":"Under sixteen must come with an adult, so a twelve-year-old cannot go alone.","tr":"On altı yaş altı bir yetişkinle gelmeli; on iki yaşındaki biri tek başına katılamaz.","fa":"زیر شانزده سال باید با یک بزرگسال بیاید، پس بچه‌ی دوازده‌ساله نمی‌تواند تنها برود."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Lunch is provided on the coastal tours.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"including a stop for lunch on a small beach","why":{"en":"There is a lunch stop, but the text does not say who provides the food.","tr":"Öğle yemeği molası var ama yemeği kimin sağladığı söylenmiyor.","fa":"توقفی برای ناهار هست، اما نمی‌گوید غذا را چه کسی می‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Customers whose tour is cancelled can get their money back.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"you can choose a full refund","why":{"en":"\"A full refund\" = your money back.","tr":"\"Tam iade\" = paranı geri almak.","fa":"«بازپرداخت کامل» یعنی پولت را پس می‌گیری."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Any adult can hire a kayak from the centre.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"only by people who hold a recognised paddling certificate","why":{"en":"Only people with a certificate or a completed course can hire one.","tr":"Yalnızca sertifikası olanlar ya da kurs bitirenler kiralayabilir.","fa":"فقط کسانی که مدرک دارند یا دوره را گذرانده‌اند می‌توانند کرایه کنند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The instructors are trained to give first aid.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"first-aid certificates","why":{"en":"All instructors hold \"first-aid certificates\".","tr":"Bütün eğitmenlerin \"ilk yardım sertifikası\" var.","fa":"همه‌ی مربی‌ها «گواهی کمک‌های اولیه» دارند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The car park is usually full by mid-morning.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"the car park is small, so please share cars where possible","why":{"en":"It is \"small\", but nothing is said about when it fills up.","tr":"\"Küçük\" deniyor ama ne zaman dolduğundan söz edilmiyor.","fa":"گفته «کوچک است»، اما چیزی درباره‌ی زمان پر شدنش نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]}]}],"id":"c-x08-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"A review says the boots needed \"no breaking in\". This means they were...","options":["impossible to damage","easy to put on","comfortable from the start"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Breaking in = wearing new shoes until they become comfortable.","tr":"Breaking in = yeni ayakkabıyı rahat olana kadar giymek.","fa":"breaking in یعنی کفش نو را آن‌قدر بپوشی تا راحت شود."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"you can get your money back\". Which words in an advert mean the same?","options":["a small deposit","a full refund","a discount for groups"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A refund = money paid back to you.","tr":"Refund = sana geri ödenen para.","fa":"refund یعنی پولی که به تو برگردانده می‌شود."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Seven statements and six reviews (A-F). What does this tell you?","options":["At least one letter is the answer twice","One statement has no answer","Each letter is used once"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Seven answers from six letters: at least one letter repeats.","tr":"Altı harften yedi cevap: en az bir harf tekrar eder.","fa":"هفت جواب از شش حرف: دست‌کم یک حرف تکرار می‌شود."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Children under ten must wear a helmet.\" Statement: \"Adults are not allowed to wear helmets.\"","options":["FALSE","TRUE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The rule is about children; the text says nothing about adults.","tr":"Kural çocuklarla ilgili; metin yetişkinler hakkında bir şey söylemiyor.","fa":"قانون درباره‌ی بچه‌هاست؛ متن درباره‌ی بزرگسال‌ها چیزی نمی‌گوید."}}],"id":"c-x08-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-08","unit":"x08-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
